WEBVTT

00:15:56.337 --> 00:16:01.257
that required the OMB
score every piece of legislation

00:16:01.257 --> 00:16:02.537
for its carbon impact.

00:16:02.537 --> 00:16:03.537
HH: Yes.

00:16:03.537 --> 00:16:06.810
JD: If we're serious about this,
we're going to measure what matters,

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:08.306
measure what really matters.

00:16:08.306 --> 00:16:09.303
HH: Yup. Yup.

00:16:09.303 --> 00:16:11.637
JD: So let's talk about Paris
and the Paris Accord

00:16:11.637 --> 00:16:16.023
because some people say that some
nations are ahead of their plans,

00:16:16.023 --> 00:16:17.660
but others are not,

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:21.977
and that the agenda
is not aggressive enough.

00:16:21.977 --> 00:16:24.157
It’s not going to get us
where we need to go.

00:16:24.157 --> 00:16:27.500
What is your view of the Paris Accords?

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.943
HH: The Paris Accords
are quite interesting animals.